# Goal 7: Fix modf NaN handling

## Function
modf (split into integer and fractional parts, double)

## Source Files
- C source: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/modfd.c
- Rust source: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s5/src/mathd.rs

## What's Wrong
modf(nan) returns wrong fractional part:
- C:    modf(nan) = nan, ip=nan
- Rust: modf(nan) = 0x0p+0, ip=nan

The integer part is correct (nan), but the fractional part should also be nan. The Rust code likely has a code path that returns 0.0 for the fractional part when the input is NaN, instead of returning NaN.

## What Needs to Change
Check the NaN handling path in modf. When input is NaN, both the integer part and the fractional part should be NaN. The C code likely returns x (which is NaN) for the fractional part.

## Success Criteria
- modf(nan) returns nan for both fractional and integer parts
- All modf test cases match C output bitwise
